.TH 121GW\-QT 1 "2026-11-03" "121gw-qt 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
121gw\-qt \- front panel, remote control and MCP server for the EEVblog 121GW multimeter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 121gw\-qt
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 121gw\-qt
connects to an EEVblog 121GW multimeter over Bluetooth Low Energy and shows its whole
front panel live: the LCD, the rotary dial, the buttons and the input jacks, lighting the
jacks the probe leads belong in for the current mode.
Buttons pressed in the window are pressed on the meter.
Readings can be logged and saved as sessions.
.PP
With the meter's custom firmware the
.B SD card
tab lists, downloads and uploads files on the meter's card (YMODEM over Bluetooth, about
190 bytes per second) and uploads firmware images for the meter's bootloader.
Overwriting a file, and every firmware upload, waits for SETUP to be pressed on the meter.
.PP
An MCP server on
.B http://127.0.0.1:47121/mcp
(this computer only, Bearer token) lets an AI assistant read the meter, press its buttons
and suggest a dial position and jacks for a measurement.
.PP
Turn on the meter's Bluetooth by holding
.B 1ms PEAK
until
.B BT
shows, then press
.B Scan.
Without arguments the program scans for the meter used last and connects to it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Start with a simulated meter instead of Bluetooth.
Its in\-memory SD card works at the real meter's speed.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mcp
Do not start the MCP server.
.TP
.BI \-\-mcp\-port " port"
Listen for MCP on this port of 127.0.0.1 (default 47121, or the saved setting).
.TP
.B \-\-print\-mcp\-command
Print the
.B claude mcp add
command that registers this meter's MCP server, token included, and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-qml " dir"
Load the front panel from
.IR dir /main.qml
instead of
.I ~/.config/121gw\-qt/qml
or the built\-in one.
.TP
.B \-\-export\-qml
Copy the built\-in QML to
.I ~/.config/121gw\-qt/qml
to customize, and exit.
Files already there are left alone.
.TP
.BI \-\-face\-svg " file"
Draw the meter's face from this SVG (default
.I ~/.config/121gw\-qt/face.svg
if it exists).
.TP
.BI \-\-export\-svg " file"
Write a starter face SVG, the artwork plus one named rectangle per element, and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " file"
Save the window to a PNG after
.B \-\-screenshot\-delay
milliseconds and exit (for tests).
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot\-delay " ms"
Delay before
.B \-\-screenshot
(default 2500).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/121gw\-qt/settings.conf
The remembered meter, the MCP token and port (mode 600).
.TP
.I ~/.config/121gw\-qt/layout.json
Front panel offsets saved by the layout editor (Ctrl+E).
.TP
.I ~/.config/121gw\-qt/face.svg
Optional artwork for the meter's face.
.TP
.I ~/.config/121gw\-qt/qml/
Optional customized front panel (see
.BR \-\-export\-qml ).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/121gw\-qt/sessions/
Saved sessions,
.IR id .csv
and
.IR id .json,
the same files Readout writes.
.SH NOTES
Bluetooth goes through BlueZ over D\-Bus; no special group or capability is needed.
The BlueZ daemon
.RB ( bluetoothd )
must be running and the adapter powered on.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bluetoothctl (1)
.PP
